// Great windows high in the curtain wall's face, the fires of the halls behind them burning over the moat.
ë = great_window rise=13 on=_
// The great wall's face over the moat, seen from the long bridge: buttresses battered down into the
// lava, a fire basket on each, drains spilling slag down the stone, and gibbets hung from its top with
// the dead in them; and behind the front a smelting house's three flues. (The burnt ridge the
// fortress was quarried from stands on the northern horizon: the `ember` sky's own.)
Ŋ = slag_runnel yaw=90 on=K
Ō = wall_buttress yaw=90 on=K
Ŏ = gibbet_cages yaw=90 on=K
Ő = chimney_cluster on=^
// The fen's fouling and ruin: culverts low in the curtain wall pour the fortress's violet runoff into the
// mire, marsh-lights drift over the sink-holes, the moot's broken palisade stands in them, and the
// marsh-folk's watchtower lies fallen east of the watch-post.
Ĉ = runoff_sluice yaw=90 on=ē
ĉ = marsh_lights on=%
Č = marsh_lights on=-
č = fallen_watchtower yaw=30 on=-
Ė = rotten_palisade on=%
